 frequency-domain metrics, frequency bands, and short-term recording conventions.","source_id":"hrv_task_force_1996","source_type":"consensus_guideline","title":"Heart rate variability: standards of measurement, physiological interpretation and clinical use","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8598068/"},{"citation":"Jarrin DC et al. Int J Psychophysiol. 2012;86(1):88-97. doi:10.1016/j.ijpsycho.2012.07.004.","limitation":"Its inter-software ICC results are not per-metric numerical error limits for Synsigra's exact synthetic truth.","relevance":"Demonstrates that processing choices affect cross-software HRV agreement, with especially poor VLF correspondence.","source_id":"jarrin_et_al_2012","source_type":"primary_research","title":"Measurement fidelity of heart rate variability signal processing: the devil is in the details","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22820268/"},{"citation":"Salo MA et al. Ann Noninvasive Electrocardiol. 2001;6(1):5-17. PMID:11174857.","limitation":"It does not prescribe Synsigra's NN exclusion policy or numerical acceptance gates.","relevance":"Shows that ectopic-beat editing method and burden materially affect time- and frequency-domain HRV results.","source_id":"salo_et_al_2001","source_type":"primary_research","title":"Ectopic beats in heart rate variability analysis: effects of editing on time and frequency domain measures","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11174857/"}]},"evidence_boundary":"Synthetic engineering QA evidence for RR and HRV implementation; not diagnosis, clinical autonomic validation, patient-population evidence, or regulatory qualification.","evidence_profile":{"description":"The curated pack's reviewed engineering acceptance gates for mature implementations. This is the recommended default.","display_name":"Level 2 \u2014 Advanced","policy_contract":"synsigra_evidence_profile_policy_v1","profile_id":"level_2","rank":2,"threshold_adjustment":"The pack author's reviewed baseline thresholds are used unchanged.